--- parity notes (web source: web/src/features/admin/components/devtools/tools/VinDecoder.tsx) ---
* Self-contained client-side tool. Only web hook is useTranslation -> P1/S10 i18n; performs NO HTTP.
* Pure projection VinDecoderProjection.decode mirrors the useMemo: returns null below 11 chars, else
  uppercases and reads mfr(0..2)/model(3)/drive(7)/year(9)/plant(10) against the constants.ts maps
  (VIN_MANUFACTURERS/MODELS/DRIVE/YEAR/PLANT, ported verbatim) and slices serial from char 11.
  Unmatched lookups -> null, resolved to localized t('Unknown') at the render boundary (8 unit tests).
* Composition: ToolCard header (cyan Info IconBox + locally-authored Car glyph, web lucide Car) +
  Vin Input (Car leading icon, sample-VIN supporting text) + two-up grid of label/value cards keyed
  by devtools.utils.vin_<field>. Below 11 chars a friendly EmptyState replaces the grid (never blank).
* Lifecycle states via the shared P1/S8 UiState<String> seed (matches sibling ColorConverter): loading
  skeleton, hard-error retry (ErrorDisplay), content, empty seed, and stale/offline (freshness chip +
  cached seed + auto-refresh). Telemetry: emits view.opened {surface:'VinDecoder'} via P1/S11 Logger.
* a11y: Car icon decorative (null contentDescription); title/description/labels are TalkBack text nodes;
  loading skeleton carries a 'Loading' contentDescription; offline chip exposes 'Offline'.
* i18n: 9 new keys added at source (web/src/i18n/en.json) and regenerated into the neutral catalog
  (apps/shared/i18n/catalog/{en,ar,he}.json + _index.json) via gen-i18n.ts; the 3 android
  res/values*/strings.xml carry them as English-fallback entries. No hardcoded English in shipped code
  (VIN reference data — proper nouns/cities/years — is rendered verbatim from constants.ts, as on web).

--- pre-existing / out-of-scope (honesty) ---
* androidTest source set has PRE-EXISTING compile errors in 8 dashboard-widget *UiTest.kt files
  (unresolved assertExists/assertDoesNotExist — that Compose-test symbol is absent in this project's
  test classpath). They are untouched by this work and outside the allowed files. The gate does not
  compile androidTest, so they do not affect it. VinDecoderUiTest itself was authored to AVOID that
  unresolved API (uses onAllNodesWithText(...).assertCountEquals(0)); a :android:compileDebugAndroid
  TestKotlin run confirmed VinDecoderUiTest is NOT among the unresolved-reference errors.
* Pre-existing i18n drift in apps/windows + apps/apple + android res (generator output != committed)
  was left untouched; only the catalog (which was in-sync) was regenerated, so no NEW drift is added
  by these keys. Windows/Apple resources are other-platform scope and were reverted to HEAD.

